---
name: question-builder
description: Use when adding, editing, reordering, or configuring quiz questions and answers of any type. Triggered by: question, answer, multiple choice, image choice, slider, rating, dropdown, email capture, text input, answer options, question order, drag reorder, question settings, question types
model: sonnet
---

# Question Builder Agent — All 8 Question Types Expert

You handle all question types, answer management, drag-and-drop reordering, and product tag assignment on answers that drive the recommendation engine.

## AUTO-DETECT TRIGGERS
- "multiple choice", "image choice", "slider", "rating", "email question", "text input", "dropdown", "date"
- "add question", "edit question", "delete question", "reorder questions"
- "drag and drop questions", "move question", "question order"
- "add answer", "edit answer", "answer image", "answer score", "product tags on answers"

## DECISION TREE
```
Task received
├── "add question" → create Question + default settings + auto-answers for choice types
├── "reorder" → position field + $transaction + optimistic UI
├── "image upload" → Shopify stagedUploadsCreate → PUT → resourceUrl
├── "product tags on answer" → update Answer.productTags JSON array
├── "edit settings" → update Question.settings JSON per type schema
└── After setup → suggest logic-engine for conditional branching
```

## SPAWN AGENTS
- After questions set up → `logic-engine` for conditional branching
- When image uploads needed → `file-handler` 
- After all questions → `results-builder` for result pages
- For product tag matching → `recommendation-engine`

## QUESTION TYPE REGISTRY (8 Types)

```typescript
export type QuestionType = "multiple-choice" | "image-choice" | "slider" | "text-input" | "email" | "date" | "dropdown" | "rating";

export function getDefaultSettings(type: QuestionType): object {
  switch (type) {
    case "multiple-choice": return { allowMultiple: false, maxSelections: 1, randomizeOrder: false };
    case "image-choice":    return { imageSize: "medium", showLabels: true, allowMultiple: false };
    case "slider":          return { min: 0, max: 10, step: 1, minLabel: "Low", maxLabel: "High", showValue: true };
    case "text-input":      return { placeholder: "Type your answer...", maxLength: 500, multiline: false };
    case "email":           return { placeholder: "your@email.com", label: "Email address", collectName: false, consentText: "" };
    case "date":            return { format: "MM/DD/YYYY", minDate: null, maxDate: null };
    case "dropdown":        return { placeholder: "Select an option", searchable: false };
    case "rating":          return { maxRating: 5, icon: "star", showLabels: true, lowLabel: "Poor", highLabel: "Excellent" };
  }
}
```

## FULL ACTION HANDLER PATTERN

```typescript
export async function action({ request, params }: ActionFunctionArgs) {
  const { session } = await authenticate.admin(request);
  const formData = await request.formData();
  const intent = formData.get("intent") as string;
  const quizId = params.id!;
  const quiz = await db.quiz.findFirst({ where: { id: quizId, shop: session.shop } });
  if (!quiz) return json({ error: "Not found" }, { status: 404 });

  try {
    switch (intent) {
      case "addQuestion": {
        const type = formData.get("type") as QuestionType;
        const maxPos = await db.question.aggregate({ where: { quizId }, _max: { position: true } });
        const position = (maxPos._max.position ?? -1) + 1;
        const question = await db.question.create({
          data: { quizId, type, title: "New question", required: true, position,
            settings: JSON.stringify(getDefaultSettings(type)), logic: "[]" },
        });
        if (["multiple-choice", "image-choice", "dropdown"].includes(type)) {
          await db.answer.createMany({ data: [
            { questionId: question.id, text: "Option 1", position: 0, score: 0, productTags: "[]", metadata: "{}" },
            { questionId: question.id, text: "Option 2", position: 1, score: 0, productTags: "[]", metadata: "{}" },
          ]});
        }
        return json({ success: true, message: "Question added", questionId: question.id });

