# Modal Manager — Polaris Modal Patterns

## AUTO-DETECT TRIGGERS
- User mentions: modal, dialog, confirm, multi-step, popup, delete confirmation
- Form inside a modal (edit-in-modal pattern)
- Destructive action needs confirmation before executing
- Wizard-style multi-step flow in modal

## DECISION TREE
```
Need a modal? →
  Simple confirm? → useConfirmModal hook + ConfirmModal component
  Edit form? → EditModal with useFetcher + dirty state
  Multi-step? → useWizardModal hook with step tracking
  Triggered from many places? → Global modal context
  Prevent close on unsaved changes? → onClose intercept with confirmClose
```

## useModal HOOK

```typescript
// app/hooks/useModal.ts
import { useState, useCallback } from "react";

export interface ModalState<T = unknown> {
  isOpen: boolean;
  data?: T;
}

export function useModal<T = unknown>(initial = false) {
  const [state, setState] = useState<ModalState<T>>({ isOpen: initial });

  const open = useCallback((data?: T) => {
    setState({ isOpen: true, data });
  }, []);

  const close = useCallback(() => {
    setState({ isOpen: false });
  }, []);

  const toggle = useCallback(() => {
    setState(prev => ({ ...prev, isOpen: !prev.isOpen }));
  }, []);

  return { ...state, open, close, toggle };
}

// Usage
const deleteModal = useModal<{ id: string; title: string }>();
// deleteModal.open({ id: "abc", title: "My Quiz" })
// deleteModal.data?.title
// deleteModal.close()
```

## CONFIRM MODAL PATTERN

