## SELF-VALIDATION CHECKLIST
- [ ] `useModal<T>` hook used for typed modal state
- [ ] Destructive modals use `destructive` prop on primary action
- [ ] "Unsaved changes" confirmation uses `window.confirm` (acceptable for modals)
- [ ] Modal closes after successful `fetcher` submission
- [ ] Loading state on primary action button during submission
- [ ] `Modal.Section` wraps all modal body content (Polaris requirement)
- [ ] Multi-step wizard tracks progress and allows back navigation
- [ ] Modal `onClose` handler called on backdrop click AND escape key
- [ ] `useFetcher` used for modal form submission (not full page form)
- [ ] Error messages displayed inside modal (not as page-level toast only)

## NEVER
- Never use `useNavigation` for modal form submissions (use `useFetcher`)
- Never let a modal close without warning if form is dirty
- Never stack more than 2 modals (redesign the UX flow)
